    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d372">

                <pb facs="0435" n="1169" xml:id="pg1169"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Adee to Mr.
                            Dupuy de Lôme.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-07-10"><hi rendition="#italic">July 10,
                        1895</hi>.</date></dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 18.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In view of the time that has elapsed since
                    Mr. Olney’s note to you of the 22d ultimo in regard to the Mora claim, and
                    having reference not only to your written reply of the 25th ultimo, but also to
                    the confirmation thereof by the oral assurances given by you to the Secretary of
                    State that a definite and satisfactory response would be made by His Majesty’s
                    Government as soon as the text of Mr. Olney’s note of June 22 had been received
                    at Madrid by mail, I have the honor to inquire whether you are in a position to
                    make the important communication which is awaited by the President.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvey A. Adee</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
